Agent setup

Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/doutoracoelho-hub/Prontagenda.git
cd Prontagenda

Go to the agent directory:

cd ai-agent

Create a Python virtual environment:

python -m venv .venv

Activate it.

Linux / macOS:

source .venv/bin/activate

Windows:

.venv\Scripts\activate

Install dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt

Create the environment configuration based on the example file:

cp .env.example .env

Configure the required environment variables.

Example:

GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=
GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=true

PRONTAGENDA_BASE_URL=
PRONTAGENDA_AGENT_TOKEN=
PRONTAGENDA_SIGNING_SECRET=

Do not commit real credentials.

Run the agent locally

Example:

python -m app

or, depending on the implementation:

uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080

Check the health endpoint:

curl http://localhost:8080/health

Expected result:

{
  "status": "ok"
}
Docker

Build the container:

docker build -t prontagenda-ai-agent .

Run locally:

docker run -p 8080:8080 --env-file .env prontagenda-ai-agent
Deploy to Cloud Run

Example deployment:

gcloud run deploy prontagenda-ai-hackathon \
  --source . \
  --region southamerica-east1 \
  --platform managed

Production secrets should be provided through secure Google Cloud configuration and must never be committed to the repository.

