Security

Security was a core architectural requirement.

The implementation uses concepts including:

signed request context;
Bearer-token authentication;
controlled tool endpoints;
server-side business-rule validation;
no direct model-to-database access;
multi-company isolation;
human escalation;
protected environment variables;
Cloud Run service boundaries;
application audit logging.

Sensitive data such as credentials, tokens, patient data, production database dumps and private keys are excluded from the repository.

Observability

Cloud Run logs provide visibility into:

application startup;
health checks;
agent requests;
WhatsApp requests;
tool execution;
response status;
execution latency.

This allows the agent workflow to be inspected without exposing unrestricted model access to application data.

