What we learned

The biggest lesson from this project is that an effective AI agent is not defined by how much it talks.

It is defined by what it can safely accomplish.

Building an agent connected to a real application requires more than prompt engineering.

It requires:

authentication;
authorization;
tool boundaries;
deterministic business rules;
state management;
error handling;
observability;
human escalation.

The project also reinforced the importance of separating model reasoning from direct data access.

Gemini decides what should happen.

Controlled Prontagenda tools determine what is allowed to happen.

